@startuml
title Current Pain and Gain tick flow

component "src/main.mjs" as Main
component "src/loop.js" as Loop
component "src/arena/observe.js" as Observe
component "src/strategy/objectives.js" as Objectives
component "src/config.js\nsrc/strategy/secondary-objective-plan.js" as Secondary
component "src/strategy/supported-contest.js" as Contest
component "src/squads/membership.js" as Membership
component "src/config.js\nsrc/strategy/flag-allocation.js" as Allocation
component "src/config.js\nsrc/tactics/healer-escort.js" as Escort
component "src/config.js\nsrc/squads/pair.js" as Pair
component "src/debug/game-state.js" as Debug
component "src/debug/replay-evidence.js" as Evidence
component "src/arena/execute.js" as Execute
component "src/tactics/movement.js" as Movement
component "src/tactics/healer-closing.js\nhealerUsefulClosingExperiment=false" as Closing
component "src/tactics/healing.js" as Healing
component "src/tactics/combat.js" as Combat
component "src/tactics/body.js\nsrc/tactics/targets.js" as Eligibility
cloud "Screeps Arena API" as API

Main --> Loop : runTick()
Loop --> Observe : collect flags, owned creeps,\nenemies, damaged allies
Observe --> API : getObjectsByPrototype() / getTicks()
Loop --> Membership : reset on tick restart; update from\nowned pre-action creeps
Membership --> Pair : stable same-squad members\nonly when experiment enabled
Loop --> Evidence : baseline or change-only membership\nevidence after update
Membership --> Evidence : read resulting state\nwithout mutation
Loop --> Objectives : select first flag
Loop --> Secondary : default-off secondary trial;\noriginal centre + existing membership + controller exclusions
Secondary --> Objectives : unchanged pure selector;\none bounded existing-squad attempt
Secondary --> Contest : capture first refusal; isolated unarmed contest\nuses remaining shared work; same lifecycle on handoff
Secondary --> API : at most24 searchPath queries on acquisition;\n4 active refreshes, maxOps1000 each
Secondary --> Execute : shared validated first steps; capture replaces only flag fallback;\ncentre/rejoin/escort references unchanged
Secondary --> Debug : bounded game-state.secondaryObjective;\nobserved positions, not movement claims
Loop --> Execute : capture/contest whole-group preflight BEFORE snapshot/commands;\ncapture yields to combat too; priority conflict invalidates ownership
Execute --> Contest : all current/next weapon/healer combinations\nretain functioning range3 access; occupied steps wait
note right of Contest : Capture and contest use direct move(direction)\nto validated adjacent cells; all partial/stay outcomes keep support.\nCapture cancels ownership for ordinary combat approach;\ncontest may replace compatible combat approach, including handoff.\nAttack/healing selectors stay unchanged;\n24 acquisition /4 refresh queries are shared; no extra wait allowance.
Loop --> Allocation : optional one-scout fallback\n(default off; one attempt)
Allocation --> API : searchPath() terrain-route estimates\nwhen enabled
Loop --> Escort : optional one-healer pair\n(default on; one assignment)
Loop --> Pair : optional leader/follower (default off)\nescort and ordinary movement retain priority
Pair --> Execute : joint step / bounded wait;\nrelease restores ordinary movement
Loop --> Observe : sample starting map once
Observe --> API : getObjects() / getTerrainAt()
Loop --> Debug : log map once, then tick state\nbefore actions
Escort --> Debug : assignment/release diagnostic\nbefore actions
Debug --> API : console.log(JSON snapshot)
Loop --> Execute : choose and issue movement\nwith optional scout fallback / healer escort
Execute --> Movement : combat objective or pure-healer support,\nthen first flag fallback
note right of Movement : Optional scout hold (default off):\nunassigned, healthy MOVE-only scout\nwithin two of owned first flag, no nearby enemy.\nAllocation overrides and escort retain priority.
Movement --> Eligibility : functioning weapons / HEAL and range
Execute --> Closing : default-off; ordinary healer hold only AFTER owners/retreat\nknown flags, terrain, occupancy and healing/support bands
Closing --> Movement : reuse bounded eight-neighbour evaluation
Closing --> Healing : read-only current-position target selection
note right of Closing : One adjacent move(direction), no path search or new reservation.\nNo persistent closing/wait state; snapshots establish progress.\nHealing is still selected from current positions.\nConvergence may lose progress indefinitely; no survival guarantee.
note right of Movement : Pure-healer pressure retreat reuses bounded8-cell checks:\nstrictly less current weapon exposure, no new ranged source,\nno melee reach, all current injured-ally healing bands retained.\nEscort/pair owners win; no extra path search or survival guarantee.
note left of Movement : Pure-ranged adjacent-melee retreat:\nup to eight plain, free neighbour cells;\nno current melee reach or new ranged envelope.\nFull observed occupancy and local terrain supplied;\nescort/pair priority and tactical selectors unchanged.
Execute --> API : at most one move(direction) OR moveTo(target) per actor
Execute --> Debug : escort hold, fatigue pause, or move attempt\nwith actual return code
Loop --> Execute : execute tactics after movement
Execute --> Healing : choose available healing
Execute --> Combat : choose compatible attacks
note right of Combat : Guarded equal-range ranged spillover trial:\nfull observation and neutral modifiers required;\nonly earlier accepted compatible melee funds\na tick-local nominal budget. No action reordering.\nUnknown evidence keeps baseline targeting.
Healing --> Eligibility : functioning HEAL, range, target
Combat --> Eligibility : functioning ATTACK / RANGED_ATTACK,\nrange, target
Execute --> API : heal / rangedHeal / attack / rangedAttack
Loop --> API : getCpuTime() after gameplay;\nread applicable Arena CPU limit
Loop --> Evidence : runtime-cpu sample, then\nmembership/action/CPU coverage closure
Evidence --> API : console.log(versioned records)
Execute --> Evidence : decisions before original calls;\nattempts immediately after returns
note right of Evidence : M2/M3 closures remain valid;\nversion 2 adds one late CPU sample

@enduml
